Rule 2 (bias size should match the first dimension of weight)
{v_3 : tensor, v_4 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) = 3 ∧ ndim(v_4) = 1 ∧ shape(v_3, 0) = shape(v_4, 0)
>>
Rule 3 (input1 and input2 should have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 4 (Input1 and Input2 number of features should match the weight dimensions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : tensor} |= ndim(v_3) = 3 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_3, 1) ∧ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1) = shape(v_3, 2)
